  { q: 'Why is humidity as important as heat for batteries in the UAE?', a: 'Coastal UAE combines summer temperatures of 40\u00b0C+ with high humidity from the Persian Gulf. Heat accelerates lead-acid ageing and water loss, while humidity and salt air promote terminal corrosion. Correct electrolyte care and corrosion-resistant terminals matter more here than inland.' },
